mment_lines":["[][148]"],"review_comment":["Because we do not directly bring in a JSON library (e.g. Gson or Jackson) we can not use the simple facilities that these libs have to \"encode a JSON string\". \r\n\r\nHere were the options:\r\n\r\n## Use JSON lib\r\nAdd required dependency on Jackson or Gson and use their built-in methods\r\n\r\n- ✅ solid encode impl maintained by JSON lib\r\n- ❌ ❌ ❌ have to bring in direct dep on JSON lib and this forces it upon our users (not an option)\r\n \r\n## Add feature to Spring Boot JsonParser\r\nAdd \"encode a JSON string\" to our `JsonParser` abstraction\r\n\r\n- ✅ can be used in other areas of Spring Boot codebase\r\n- ❌ created and maintained by us (more work)\r\n- ❌ impl no more solid than if it were a private impl inside the mapper\r\n- ❌ nowhere else in the Boot codebase needs this AFAIK\r\n \r\n## Hand-roll basic encoder\r\nInline a simple encode JSON facility in the mapper.\r\n\r\n- ❌ basic impl maintained by us\r\n- ❌ ✅ not a perfect solution but will solve the majority of the cases\r\n- ✅ ✅ no direct dep on JSON lib\r\n- ✅ private impl localized to the mapper\r\n\r\n"],"path":"spring-boot-project/spring-boot-autoconfigure/src/main/java/org/springframework/boot/autoconfigure/pulsar/PulsarPropertiesMapper.java","id":14083,"created_at":"2024-04-23T23:34:13Z","original_position":13,"side":"RIGHT","position":13,"submitted_on_commit":"df1845c4baa1d6707c6e0657cd7c9d46245f570f","diff_hunk":"@@ -137,14 +137,25 @@ private String getAuthenticationParamsJson(Map\u003cString, String\u003e params) {\n \t\ttry {\n \t\t\treturn sortedParams.entrySet()\n \t\t\t\t.stream()\n-\t\t\t\t.map((entry) -\u003e \"\\\"%s\\\":\\\"%s\\\"\".formatted(entry.getKey(), entry.getValue()))\n+\t\t\t\t.map((entry) -\u003e \"\\\"%s\\\":\\\"%s\\\"\".formatted(entry.getKey(), escapeJson(entry.getValue())))\n \t\t\t\t.collect(Collectors.joining(\",\", \"{\", \"}\"));\n \t\t}\n \t\tcatch (Exception ex) {\n \t\t\tthrow new IllegalStateException(\"Could not convert auth parameters to encoded string\", ex);\n \t\t}\n \t}\n \n+\tprivate String escapeJson(String raw) {","submitted_line":148},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The introduction of the `escapeJson` method and its usage in `getAuthenticationParamsJson` diverges from the mapping\u0027s logic in terms of handling certain edge cases and potential security vulnerabilities. The current implementation of `escapeJson` only handles a specific set of escape sequences (e.g., `\\`, `\"`, `/`, `\\b`, `\\t`, `\\n`, `\\f`, `\\r`) and does not account for all possible characters that need to be escaped in JSON, such as Unicode characters. This could lead to malformed JSON or security vulnerabilities if such characters are present in the input strings. Additionally, the mapping does not specify how `escapeJson` should handle nested JSON structures, yet the test cases include complex parameters with nested JSON. While the current implementation might work for simple cases, it may fail to correctly escape characters within nested JSON strings, leading to potential security issues or malformed JSON.","nodes":[{"id":"spring-boot-project/spring-boot-autoconfigure/src/test/java/org/springframework/boot/autoconfigure/pulsar/PulsarPropertiesMapperTests.java-DST-ADDITION-8251-8397-VariableDeclarationStatement","path":"spring-boot-project/spring-boot-autoconfigure/src/test/java/org/springframework/boot/autoconfigure/pulsar/PulsarPropertiesMapperTests.java","srcDst":"DST","content":"String authParamString \u003d \"{\\\"complexParam\\\":\\\"{\\\\n\\\\t\\\\\\\"k1\\\\\\\" : \\\\\\\"v1\\\\\\\",\\\\n\\\\t\\\\\\\"k2\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"v2\\\\\\\"\\\\n}\\\"\"\n\t\t\t\t+ \",\\\"simpleParam\\\":\\\"foo\\\"}\";","nodeType":"ADDITION","treeType":"VariableDeclarationStatement","descendantSimpleNames":["String","authParamString"],"identifiers":["authParamString"],"startLine":173,"startLineOffset":2,"endLine":174,"endLineOffset":34,"length":147,"subs":[]},{"id":"spring-boot-project/spring-boot-autoconf